<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Results</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A3.F6" title="In Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Measuring Scalar Constructs in Social Science with LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows the distribution of LLM confidences in the most-probable (modal) response over multiple model types and prompting strategies.
Any given design decision can have a large impact on confidence.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.03116v1/figure06.svg" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/153;" width="476" height="153"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>LLM confidence in the modal response varies widely over model variants and prompting strategy, leading to inconsistent behavior that can impact downstream conclusions.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Measuring Scalar Constructs in Social Science with LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> compares the pointwise scoring performance of the two open-weights models we use to the performance of GPT-4o based on the Ad-Negativity data.
Table <a href="#A3.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Measuring Scalar Constructs in Social Science with LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows that our prompting results for pointwise scoring with token probability weighting are robust to running inference without 4-bit quantization.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Comparison of pointwise scoring prompting results between open-weights and proprietary models in Ad-Negativity data. <em id="A3.T8.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Notes:</em> Metrics reported are the pair classification accuracy (Acc) and scoring performance relative to ground-truth BT scores in terms of Spearman’s rank correlation (<math id="A3.T8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>) and the root mean squared error (RMSE, on scale 0–1). Values report are averages <math id="A3.T8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> one standard deviation computed by summarizing results across five folds.</figcaption>
