</figure>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Complementing the selected results highlighted in <a href="#S4.F5" title="In Pointwise outperforms pairwise prompting. ‣ 4.1 Prompting ‣ 4 Results ‣ Measuring Scalar Constructs in Social Science with LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>,
<a href="#A3.F7" title="In Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Measuring Scalar Constructs in Social Science with LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows the relation between model responses and ground-truth BT scores in prompted models’ probability-weighted average pointwise scores (5-shot), and
<a href="#A3.F8" title="In Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Measuring Scalar Constructs in Social Science with LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> the relation between predicted scores and ground-truth BT scores in models fine-tuned on all examples in datasets’ training splits.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A3.F9" title="In Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Measuring Scalar Constructs in Social Science with LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, in turn, shows how finetuned models’ classification and scoring performance changes with the number of training examples used for finetuning.
<a href="#A3.F10" title="In Appendix C Additional Results ‣ Measuring Scalar Constructs in Social Science with LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> contrasts finetuned reward models’ performance with those of regression models finetuned using inferred BT scores instead of pairwise label data.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.03116v1/figure07.svg" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:476/638;" width="476" height="638"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>
Relation between model responses and ground-truth BT scores in prompted models’ probability-weighted average pointwise scores (5-shot).
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.03116v1/figure08.svg" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/400;" width="476" height="400"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>
Relation between model responses and ground-truth BT scores in models fine-tuned on all examples in datasets’ training splits (
2,729 in the <span id="A3.F8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Immigration Fear</span>,
6,760 in the <span id="A3.F8.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Ad-Negativity</span>,
and
32,308 in the <span id="A3.F8.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Immigration Fear</span>data).
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<figure id="A3.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.03116v1/figure09.svg" id="A3.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/277;" width="476" height="277"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>
Classification and scoring performance of finetuned models as a function of the number of training examples.
“all” refers to all pairs in the training split (
2,729 in the <span id="A3.F9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Immigration Fear</span>,
6,760 in the <span id="A3.F9.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Ad-Negativity</span>,
and
32,308 in the <span id="A3.F9.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Immigration Fear</span>data).
Points and vertical bars report averages ± one standard deviation computed by summarizing results across five folds.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F10" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.03116v1/figure10.svg" id="A3.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/280;" width="476" height="280"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>
Classification and scoring performance of finetuned reward and regression models as a function of the number of training examples.
Results shown for finetunes of <span id="A3.F10.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">deberta-v3-large</span>.
“all” refers to all pairs in the training split (
2,729 in the <span id="A3.F10.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Immigration Fear</span>,
6,760 in the <span id="A3.F10.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Ad-Negativity</span>,
and
32,308 in the <span id="A3.F10.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Immigration Fear</span>data).
Points and vertical bars report averages ± one standard deviation computed by summarizing results across five folds.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
